WEBVTT

00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:17,070
With deciding on regular blood work, what should I choose?

00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:22,070
Typically, it depends on your case.

00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:26,070
So everybody is going to be different as far as what I would recommend for blood work.

00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:31,070
But in general, everybody should be getting a CBC with differential.

00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:38,070
That's a complete blood count with differential and a comprehensive metabolic profile.

00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:40,070
I'm a standard metabolic profile.

00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:44,070
Lots of times if you go to your doctor or let's say you have Medicare,

00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:47,070
they're going to run the cheapest blood work as possible.

00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:50,070
Ask for a comprehensive metabolic profile.

00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:56,070
If I haven't done record, if I have an order of blood work on somebody before

00:00:56,070 --> 00:00:59,070
and looked at their thyroid, typically when I order the blood work

00:00:59,070 --> 00:01:03,070
or also order a complete thyroid panel,

00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:08,070
because we want to differentiate between somebody who has, you know,

00:01:08,070 --> 00:01:13,070
either a very hypo thyroid condition that has never been diagnosed

00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:16,070
and or a Hashimoto's that has never been diagnosed,

00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:21,070
versus somebody that's having a lot of fatigue from an anemia.

00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:26,070
So anemia obviously is very common with cancer, but many cancer patients,

00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:30,070
the diagnosis cancer have never actually had complete blood work

00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:35,070
to even diagnose whether they had a comorbidity of low thyroid issue.

00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:40,070
So I always like to screen for that and rule that out once we see that

00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:45,070
that is within normal range than typically the second blood work that I'll order

00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:51,070
for a person that I would omit that, and I might run some other tests.

00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:55,070
Also, if you have cancer and you haven't had tuber markers done,

00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:58,070
then running a tuber marker panel can be valuable.

00:01:58,070 --> 00:02:02,070
If you're a female, obviously the female or the male tuber marker panel

00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:04,070
added to that as well.

00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:08,070
That would be just general blood work that we would look at

00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:13,070
that would give us clues that I have made a lot of videos and blog posts

00:02:13,070 --> 00:02:17,070
about a lot of those markers that you'd find in that panel,

00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:22,070
in those panels that I just discussed and what they would mean.

00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:24,070
If you want more information on tuber markers,

00:02:24,070 --> 00:02:28,070
then you can look up the blog post on tuber markers,

00:02:28,070 --> 00:02:35,070
and there's an exhaustive information on that and videos on that as well.

00:02:35,070 --> 00:02:39,070
But obviously there's a lot of other blood work that could be run to help

00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:45,070
diagnose a different conditioner to help figure out something else that's going on as well.

